hadiths[18]{hadithnumber,text}:
"433","Sayyiduna Ya'la bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I said to Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that Allah Almighty says: ""There is no sin on you if you shorten the prayer if you fear that the disbelievers may harm you"" (An-Nisa: 101), and now people are in peace (i.e., is shortening the prayer still permissible or not?). He said: I was also surprised as you are surprised, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this matter. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is a charity that Allah has given you, so accept His charity (i.e., shorten the prayer during travel even without fear)."
"434","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` Allah Almighty prescribed through the tongue of your Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) four rak‘ahs in residence, two in travel, and one rak‘ah in fear."
"435","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I offered four rak‘ahs of Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, and I offered two rak‘ahs of ‘Asr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Dhul-Hulaifah."
"436","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we set out from Madinah to Makkah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he continued to perform two rak‘ahs (for each prayer) until he returned. I asked, ""How many days did you stay in Makkah?"" He said, ""Ten days."" In another narration, it is mentioned that we set out from Madinah to (Makkah) for Hajj."
"437","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the prayer of a traveler in Mina, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) also did so, and Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) also performed the prayer of a traveler for eight years (or he said: for six years). Hafs (i.e., Ibn Asim) said that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would perform two rak‘ahs in Mina and then come to his bedding, so I said: O my uncle! If only you would perform two more rak‘ahs after the obligatory (i.e., the Sunnah)? He replied: If I were to do so, I would complete my obligatory prayer."
"438","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, was in a hurry during a journey, he would delay Zuhr until the beginning time of Asr arrived, then combine both. And he would delay Maghrib until when the twilight disappeared, he would combine it with Isha."
"439","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) combined the Zuhr and Asr prayers and the Maghrib and Isha prayers in Madinah without fear or rain. In Waki’s narration, it is mentioned that I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), “Why did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) do this?” He replied, “So that his Ummah would not face hardship.” And in the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, it is mentioned that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked, “With what intention did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) do this?” He replied, “He did it with the intention that his Ummah should not face difficulty.”"
"440","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he gave the call to prayer (adhan) for the people on a cold, windy, and rainy night, and at the end of the adhan he said: ""Pray in your homes, pray in your homes."" Then he said that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on a journey on a cold and rainy night, he would instruct the mu'adhdhin to announce among the people: ""Pray in your tents."
"441","Hafs bin Asim said: I was with Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) on the way to Makkah, so he led us in two rak'ahs of Zuhr prayer. Then he went on and we went with him until we reached our place of stay and sat down, and we sat with him. Suddenly, his gaze fell upon the place where the prayer had been performed, and he saw some people standing. He asked, ""What are they doing?"" I said, ""They are offering Sunnah prayers."" He said, ""If I had to offer Sunnah, I would have completed the prayer (i.e., performed the full four rak'ahs of the obligatory prayer)."" Then he said, ""O nephew! I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during travel, and he never prayed more than two rak'ahs as long as he lived. I also accompanied Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and he too never prayed more than two rak'ahs as long as he lived. I also accompanied Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he too never prayed more than two rak'ahs as long as he lived. I also accompanied Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), and he too never prayed more than two rak'ahs as long as he lived. And Allah Almighty has said that in the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) there is a good example for you."
"442","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to offer voluntary prayers on his mount, regardless of which direction it was facing (it is preferable that at the beginning the mount faces the Qiblah)."
"443","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a battle, and my camel delayed and became tired, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived before me, and I reached the mosque the next day and found him at the door of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Have you just arrived?"" I said, ""Yes."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Leave your camel and go into the mosque and perform two rak‘ahs."" Then I went and performed two rak‘ahs and came back."
"444","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we fought in jihad with a tribe of Banu Juhainah in the company of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). They fought us very fiercely. Then, when we had performed the Zuhr prayer, the polytheists said, ""If only we launched a sudden attack on them, we would cut them down."" Jibreel informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) of this, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned it to us. And he said that the polytheists (also) said, ""They have another prayer coming which is dearer to them than their children."" Then, when the time for Asr came, we formed two rows (one behind the other), and the polytheists were facing the Qiblah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said the opening Takbeer, and we all said it as well. He (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed in Ruku', so we also bowed (i.e., both rows participated up to Ruku'), and he (peace and blessings be upon him) and the people of the first row performed the prostration (Sajdah). Then, when he (peace and blessings be upon him) and the first row stood up, the second row performed the prostration, and the front row moved to the back and the back row came forward. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said Allahu Akbar, and we also said it, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) bowed in Ruku', so we also bowed, and the people of the first row performed the prostration with him (peace and blessings be upon him), and the people of the second row remained standing as they were. Then, when the others had also performed the prostration, all sat down. And all of us said the Salam with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Abu az-Zubair said that Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) also said another thing: ""Just as your rulers nowadays perform the prayer."
"445","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), there was a solar eclipse. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up for prayer and stood for a very long time. Then he bowed (ruku’) and performed a very long bowing. Then he raised his head and stood for a long time, but less than the first standing. Then he bowed and performed a long bowing, but less than the first bowing. Then he prostrated (sajdah). (There were two bowings in one rak’ah, and this is also the view of Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him.) Then he stood up and stood for a long time, but less than the previous standing. Then he bowed and performed a long bowing, but less than the previous bowing. Then he raised his head and stood for a long time, but less than the previous standing. Then he bowed and performed a long bowing, but less than the previous bowing. (There were also two bowings here.) Then he prostrated and finished, and by that time the sun had become clear. Then he delivered a sermon to the people, praised and glorified Allah, and said: “The sun and the moon are among the signs of Allah, and they do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. So when you see an eclipse, glorify Allah, supplicate to Him, pray, and give charity. O Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! There is no one more possessive than Allah regarding His servant or maidservant committing adultery. O Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! By Allah! If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little. Listen! Have I not conveyed the command of Allah?”"
"446","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` when the solar eclipse occurred, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed (two rak‘ahs of prayer) with eight bowings (ruku‘) and four prostrations (sajdah)."
"447","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the Eid ground and prayed for rain. And when he intended to supplicate, he faced the Qiblah and turned his cloak inside out. And in another narration, it is mentioned that (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his back to the people and began to supplicate to Allah, and faced the Qiblah and turned his cloak inside out, then he offered two units of prayer."
"448","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when it rained upon us, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) removed his garment until the rainwater reached him. We said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Why did you do this? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Because it has just now come from its Lord."
"449","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that it was the noble habit of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that when a strong wind would blow, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite this supplication: “O Allah, I ask You for the goodness of this wind, the goodness within it, and the goodness of what it has been sent with. And I seek refuge with You from its evil, the evil within it, and the evil of what it has been sent with.” And Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when clouds appeared in the sky and there was thunder and lightning, (out of fear) the color of the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) face would change, and sometimes he would go outside, sometimes come inside, sometimes move forward, and sometimes move backward. Then, if it started to rain, the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) anxiety would go away. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I recognized this from the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so I asked him about it, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Aisha! I fear that it may be as it was with the people of ‘Ad, who saw: ‘This is a cloud coming towards us,’ and they said, ‘This cloud will bring us rain,’ (but it was the punishment coming upon them).”"
"450","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was helped (by Allah’s command) with the east wind (Bād al-Sabā), and (the people of) ‘Ād were destroyed by the west wind (Dabūr)."
